    <item>
      <title>regsensitivity Package in R</title>
      <link>https://mikenguyen.netlify.app/software/regsensitivity/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://mikenguyen.netlify.app/software/regsensitivity/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;An R package for sensitivity analysis of linear regression coefficients when omitted variables may bias them. It reports how far a coefficient can move as the no-omitted-variables assumption is relaxed, the breakdown point at which a conclusion stops holding, and plots of both, following Diegert, Masten and Poirier (2026), Oster (2019), and Masten and Poirier (2026).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Install from CRAN with &lt;code&gt;install.packages(&amp;quot;regsensitivity&amp;quot;)&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://CRAN.R-project.org/package=regsensitivity&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;CRAN&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&#34;https://mikenguyen13.github.io/regsensitivity/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Website/Vignette&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/mikenguyen13/regsensitivity&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;GitHub&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
    </item>
    
